editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/manuscript/chapter-04.md:67:"You could live there," Hesk agreed. "Inside the same walls, three streets from the Compact's district office, which checks that quarter every month, with every gate in this city pulling your record each time you pass it. And a review doesn't count houses, Cael. It counts people. A [SHATTERED] boy sleeping by the tanneries and working at his grandfather's bench all day is still a boy at 14 Fen Street, as far as the review is concerned." He shook his head. "In Denvash, the record is always waiting for you at the next gate. Ardenmere's Unranked District doesn't have one."
