editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/manuscript/chapter-04.md-142-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/manuscript/chapter-04.md:143:He thought about how many people had sat in this chair over however many years the archive had stood, reading something that applied to someone they loved, while the room kept no trace of a single one of them, having only its shelves and its dust and the patience of paper, which outlasts everyone who ever needs it.
