editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/manuscript/chapter-04.md-187-"I left the division eighteen months later," he said. "Thirty-two years I've wondered, and no answer. What I do have is a name I've never said to anyone, and a promise I made myself the day I mustered out. You ought to know that both of them exist, even if I can't give you the ending yet."
